WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.935
Day one is a check, not a lesson.

2
00:00:02.385 --> 00:00:05.041
It shows you where your child is, and where to start.

3
00:00:05.741 --> 00:00:09.853
You hold the grown-up page. Your child gets the page with the big words.

4
00:00:10.303 --> 00:00:11.482
There are three parts.

5
00:00:11.932 --> 00:00:17.189
Part A. Six words from Cap to Cape. These are the base. Mark each word read right.

6
00:00:17.639 --> 00:00:22.764
Part B. Eight words with the teams of days two to four. Mark each word read right.

7
00:00:23.214 --> 00:00:28.215
Part C. Six harder words, from days six to nine. Mark each word read right.

8
00:00:28.665 --> 00:00:36.563
Listen for one thing. If your child reads the two letters of a team apart, circle that word. That is the habit this plan works on.

9
00:00:37.263 --> 00:00:40.935
Do not teach, and do not correct today. Just listen and mark.

10
00:00:41.385 --> 00:00:46.627
Then read the box at the bottom of your page, from the top. Stop at the first line that fits.

11
00:00:47.077 --> 00:00:52.592
That line tells you where to start. It may be day two, or day six, or the story on day nine.

12
00:00:53.042 --> 00:00:58.767
One line is for the child who finds the base words hard. That child needs Cap to Cape first.

13
00:00:59.217 --> 00:01:03.895
Write the three numbers on the page, and keep it. You will look at it again on the last day.
